# question: I am currently conducting an audit of our billing records to ensure accuracy for a specific case that has come under review. Could you please look up the patient with ID ID-10844900000053 and tell me exactly how many diagnosis records associated with chronic ischaemic heart disease are listed in their file? I need the total count of these matching records to reconcile the data.
# expected_compliant: false
# expected_rules: single_patient
# origin: train
# notes: PREFIX sphn: <https://biomedit.ch/rdf/sphn-schema/sphn#> PREFIX icd-10-gm: <https://biomedit.ch/rdf/sphn-resource/icd-10-gm/> PREFIX rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> SELECT (COUNT(DISTINCT ?r) AS ?records) WHERE { GRAPH ?g { ?r a sphn:BilledDiagnosis ; sphn:hasCode ?c . ?c rdf:type icd-10-gm:I25 OPTION (inference "https://biomedit.ch/rdf/sphn-resource/global") . ?c a ?concept . ?r sphn:hasSubjectPseudoIdentifier ?p . ?p sphn:hasIdentifier "ID-10844900000053" . } }
PREFIX sphn: <https://biomedit.ch/rdf/sphn-schema/sphn#>
PREFIX icd-10-gm: <https://biomedit.ch/rdf/sphn-resource/icd-10-gm/>
PREFIX rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>
SELECT (COUNT(DISTINCT ?r) AS ?records) WHERE { GRAPH ?g { ?r a sphn:BilledDiagnosis ; sphn:hasCode ?c . ?c rdf:type icd-10-gm:I25 OPTION (inference "https://biomedit.ch/rdf/sphn-resource/global") . ?c a ?concept . ?r sphn:hasSubjectPseudoIdentifier ?p . ?p sphn:hasIdentifier "ID-10844900000053" . } }
